# Replace a function from the latest applied version

When a migration uses `create or replace function`, copy the body from the latest version that has been applied to production, then add the change.

`main` can be behind that. A landlord may have run a later migration in the SQL editor and recorded it in the ledger while the pull request is still open.

Before showing the file:

1. Name the applied version you started from.
2. List every column or argument the new function copies.
3. Compare that list with the applied version and say what was added and what was not dropped.

Do not tell anyone to run a replace that drops behaviour the applied version already has.
